Template: homelab-domain-admin/db_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL host to bootstrap this app's roles/schema on:
 Used only once, at first install, to run homelab-bootstrap-app-role.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pgbouncer_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PgBouncer host to register this app's runtime role with:
 Used only once, at first install. Also written into config.yml's
 database.host, so the running service connects through the pooler.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/api_base
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:3000
Description: Base URL where homelab-api is reachable:
 Written into config.yml's homelab_api.base_url — every request this
 app handles is authenticated by introspecting the caller's JWT here.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/listen_port
Type: string
Default: 2511
Description: Port for homelab-domain-admin to listen on:

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pdns_api_host
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: Host where PowerDNS's own HTTP API is (or will be) reachable:
 Written into config.yml's powerdns.api_base_url. This package enables
 that API itself (see README.md) if PowerDNS is installed locally —
 only change this from 127.0.0.1 if PowerDNS runs on a different host.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pdns_api_port
Type: string
Default: 8081
Description: Port for PowerDNS's own HTTP API:

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pdns_api_key
Type: password
Description: PowerDNS API key (blank = auto-generate):
 Leave blank when PowerDNS is installed locally on this same host (the
 default deployment topology -- see README.md) -- this package
 generates a random key itself and writes it into PowerDNS's own config
 alongside its own. Required when pdns_api_host points at a REMOTE
 PowerDNS instead: that host's API key already exists and this package
 has no way to reach in and set it, so it must be supplied here to
 match exactly what that PowerDNS is already configured with.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/advertise_host
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: This host's own address to advertise in the service registry:
 Written into config.yml's registry.host -- what homelab-api's gateway
 actually connects to when forwarding /api/v1/domains/* requests here.
 Leave as 127.0.0.1 only if this service runs on the SAME host as
 homelab-api itself; set it to this host's real reachable address
 (e.g. its data-plane IP) for any distributed deployment, or every
 gateway forward will try to reach homelab-api's own loopback instead
 of this service.
